(c) **Increased plasma HCO₃⁻ concentration**: Chronic retention of CO₂ (due to impaired ventilation) leads to compensatory metabolic alkalosis, raising HCO₃⁻ levels.  
(d) **Decreased CO transfer factor (Tco₂)**: Obstruction reduces alveolar ventilation, impairing gas exchange and lowering the efficiency of CO diffusion.  

