The selectivity arises because aldehydes are more electrophilic than esters, and $\text{NaBH}_4$ reacts preferentially with the more reactive aldehyde group under mild conditions.  

Final product: $\boxed{\text{Selective reduction of the aldehyde to form 158, leaving the ester and chloromethyl group unchanged.}}$
