  * m = mass of the gases (we will assuming 1 kg of water, so we will assuming the same mass of gas)
  * c<sub>g</sub> = specific heat of the gases (1.005 kJ/ kgK)
  * T<sub>1} = initial temperature of the gases (1100°C = 1473 K)
  * T<sub>2} = final temperature of the gases (550°C = 873 K)

*  Therefore,  ΔH = 1 kg * 1.005 kJ/ kgK * (1473 K - 873 K) = 600.5 kJ

* This heat is equal to the heat absorbed by the water.

** 2. Calculate the change in entropy of the gases:**

*  ΔS<sub>g</sub> = m * c<sub>g</sub> * ln(T₂/T₁)

